From: hmos2sweet <hmos2sweet@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: allow legacy enum conversions with newer Clang

The legacy WLAN stack mixes A_STATUS and QDF_STATUS. Clang 21 enables a
new enum-conversion warning, which WLAN's local -Werror makes fatal.
Keep the diagnostics, but do not promote this one warning to an error.
Scope the exception to WLAN and retain all other error checks.

diff --git a/drivers/staging/qcacld-3.0/Kbuild b/drivers/staging/qcacld-3.0/Kbuild
--- a/drivers/staging/qcacld-3.0/Kbuild
+++ b/drivers/staging/qcacld-3.0/Kbuild
@@ -1,3 +1,6 @@
+# Legacy WLAN status enums trigger a new diagnostic in Clang 21.
+ccflags-y += $(call cc-option,-Wno-error=implicit-enum-enum-cast)
+
 # We can build either as part of a standalone Kernel build or as
 # an external module.  Determine which mechanism is being used
 ifeq ($(MODNAME),)
